    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just burnout though. burnout implies there's something to recover from. but it's more like the well is bone dry. permanent. i feel like i've finished my story and the pages are just blank now. it feels so pointless to keep performing this version of 'living' when the essence of who i was is just... extinct. does that make sense? like, is it even worth trying to find color when the light itself is gone?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
